mbers into 16-bit integers (numbers from -32,767 to 32,767) because that's what the wav format expects. each number represents how much the speaker cone should move at a given moment. the wav header at the beginning of the file is just metadata, after that its just wikipedia information and code lol\\n\\nZ\\n\\nchris\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n3 messages\\n\\n3 members\\n\\n10 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1454324291213725811)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### What I learned in 1 day\\n\\nhtml & css\\n\\n<!DOCTYPE html> <html> <body> <h1>LearnSimply</h1> <p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Natus ducimus iusto ipsa similique aspernatur blanditiis voluptatum dolor. Architecto, nihil ut!</p> <hr> <ol> <li><a href=\\\"#c++\\\">C++</a></li> <li><a href=\\\"#java\\\">Java</a></li> <li><a href=\\\"#python\\\">Python</a></li> <li><a href=\\\"#html\\\">HTML</a></li> </ol> <h2 id=\\\"c++\\\">C++</h2> <p>Lorem ipsum dolor, sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Quam accusamus in expedita, necessitatibus molestiae sed officia temporibus numquam voluptas autem.</p> <h2 id=\\\"java\\\">Java</h2> <p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Commodi aperiam dolor eveniet, nihil doloribus nemo a eligendi ad rem mollitia veritatis minima ut.</p> <h2 id=\\\"python\\\">Python</h2> <p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Odit inventore obcaecati mollitia accusamus doloremque maxime corporis et voluptate eos culpa? Nostrum.</p> <h2 id=\\\"html\\\">HTML</h2> <p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipisicing elit. Exercitationem, ea labore. Assumenda, culpa quod. Fugit soluta incidunt error quaerat.</p> </body> </html> This is my code and I learned all that in. 1 day is it good?\\n\\nY\\n\\nY12x\\n\\nScript Kiddie!\\n\\n202 messages\\n\\n12 members\\n\\n10 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1454158089635889172)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Assembly linear regression model\\n\\nas you can guess, this is a linear regression model made in assembly. probably the most useless project ever. but i did it anyways 😄 repo link https://github.com/sasa0xx/asm-linear-regression-model\\n\\nS\\n\\nThanYx\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n0 messages\\n\\n1 members\\n\\n11 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1453834973454012602)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Audient\\n\\nhttps://audient.lovable.app Hey everyone, I built a webapp that instantly helps businesses and creators discover their ideal customers/audience. Business Mode: Find customers who are most likely to buy, map pain points, and identify where they hang out Creator Mode: Find viewers who will engage with your content, understand their desires, and get growth ideas No login required — start researching instantly Clean, mobile-friendly UI I’m exploring selling or licensing it rather than scaling myself. If this sounds like something you or someone you know could use, I can show a quick demo.\\n\\nM\\n\\n𝙰𝚜𝚑⚡\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n0 messages\\n\\n1 members\\n\\n12 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1453677779773034668)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### DoctorAppointmentApp\\n\\nThis is just a fun project I am working on to experiment more with C++, SQL, and AWS. The app pulls up a login where you login as one of the doctors from the database and then once you go in, you can set up, view or delete appointments.\\n\\nN\\n\\nDokkitheAstronaut\\n\\nCopy Paster!\\n\\n2 messages\\n\\n1 members\\n\\n13 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1453228368282779648)\\n\\n[\\n\\n![PokeAggregator](/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.discordapp.com%2Fattachments%2F1453192108088230009%2F1453192108914769980%2Fog-image.png%3Fex%3D695db19d%26is%3D695c601d%26hm%3D8055b439d4a20c5e6af276d56815ab05527f8fc5d7c6712681215baf99a1a8d5%26&w=3840&q=75)\\n\\n### PokeAggregator\\n\\nI built \\\\*\\\\*PokeAggregator\\\\*\\\\* a centralized archive that empowers Pokémon fans to effortlessly discover and explore over \\\\*\\\\*1,293\\\\*\\\\* fan-made games and ROM hacks. Tired of scouring scattered forums and sites for quality community projects? This tool solves that by aggregating detailed metadata from trusted sources like \\\\*\\\\*PokeHarbor\\\\*\\\\*, including release dates, versions, statuses (like Completed or In Progress), engines (RPGXP or GBA), and direct links to game pages all in one intuitive interface. ## Key features - \\\\*\\\\*Robust filters\\\\*\\\\* let users narrow down by status, engine, or source for targeted searches; - Sections for \\\\*\\\\*\\\"New Games\\\"\\\\*\\\\* and \\\\*\\\\*\\\"Recent Updates\\\"\\\\*\\\\* keep you ahead of the curve on fresh content; - Each entry provides gameplay insights, like estimated playtime for demos (e.g., 1.5–2 hours), making it simple to find your next adventure without the hassle. Deployed on \\\\*\\\\*Vercel\\\\*\\\\* for seamless performance, \\\\*\\\\*PokeAggregator\\\\*\\\\* transforms fragmented fan content into an organized, accessible hub that saves time and enhances the Pokémon community experience. Whether you're a player hunting demos or a creator tracking trends, it makes exploration efficient and engaging, proving that smart aggregation drives discovery. Check it out at - LIVE: \\\\[PokeAggregator\\\\](https://poke-aggregator.vercel.app/) - REPO: \\\\[Github\\\\](https://github.com/xodo2fast4u/poke-aggregator) and level up your fan game journey.\\n\\nX\\n\\nxodobyte\\n\\nVibe Coder!\\n\\n0 messages\\n\\n1 members\\n\\n13 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1453192108088230009)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### my journey into algorithmic trading and machine learning\\n\\nc++\\n\\nGemini Writeup: \\\\_\\\\_ Here is the problem I faced and the solution I built: ### 📉 The Problem: Visualizing the \\\"Black Box\\\" In algo trading and ML, the data isn't just text—it is millions of floating-point numbers (market ticks, tensor weights, probability distributions) generated at high frequency. I needed to see this data in real-time to debug my models, but the backend requirements were heavy: \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Server-Side Dependency:\\\\*\\\\* My trading engines and ML models relied on direct file system access and C++ DLLs that simply cannot run in a browser. \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Data Volume:\\\\*\\\\* A single training epoch or backtest could generate gigabytes of \\\\`Float64\\\\` arrays. ### 🛑 Why Standard Web Tech Failed (JSON) I quickly realized I couldn't use standard REST or JSON over WebSockets. \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*The Serialization Bottleneck:\\\\*\\\\* Converting a 1GB array of market ticks into JSON (text) explodes the size to \\\\*\\\\*~3GB\\\\*\\\\* and forces the CPU to burn cycles parsing strings back into numbers. \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Latency:\\\\*\\\\* For real-time trading visualization, the \\\"garbage collection pause\\\" caused by parsing massive JSON objects was unacceptable. ### ⚡ The Solution: A Custom Binary Bridge To bridge this gap, I built a custom binary RPC protocol that treats the browser like a direct extension of my server's memory. \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Zero-Copy Math:\\\\*\\\\* I implemented a system in \\\\`rpc-args.ts\\\\` and \\\\`encoding.ts\\\\` that serializes TypedArrays (like \\\\`Float64Array\\\\`) directly into binary. This allows my trading algorithms to dump raw numerical buffers into a WebSocket, which the browser reads immediately without parsing overhead. \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Remote Execution:\\\\*\\\\* I built a transport layer (\\\\`sender.ts\\\\`) that lets the client invoke server-only functions (like executing a trade via a DLL) by sending compact binary commands.\\n\\nS\\n\\nNo1\\n\\nCopy Paster!\\n\\n6 messages\\n\\n2 members\\n\\n13 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1453042627669786684)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Jsv-system\\n\\nJSV: A Simpler Way to Organize Data Tired of spreadsheet chaos but intimidated by databases? JSV offers a middle ground - structured data without complexity. What it is: · File-based system (no servers, no SQL) · Clean .jst files for your data · Simple queries with JQL language · Excel-ready .jsv exports Example .jst file: \\\\`\\\\`\\\\`jst database{ name: \\\"library\\\" } required{ \\\\* } schema{ title: {type: \\\"string\\\"} author: {type: \\\"string\\\"} read: {type: \\\"bool\\\"} } data{ {title: \\\"The Great Gatsby\\\", author: \\\"Fitzgerald\\\", read: true} } \\\\`\\\\`\\\\` Simple queries: \\\\`\\\\`\\\\`bash jsv query \\\"QUERY library.data WHERE read = false\\\" jsv query \\\"COUNT library.data\\\" \\\\`\\\\`\\\\` Perfect for: · Small business inventory · Personal collections · Research data · Any list that's outgrown spreadsheets Get started: \\\\`\\\\`\\\\`bash npm install -g jsv-system jsv init my-project \\\\`\\\\`\\\\` GitHub: https://github.com/JSV-net/jsv-system Simple, file-based, no subscriptions. Try it with one small project first.\\n\\nC\\n\\nCoderX-176-max\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n0 messages\\n\\n1 members\\n\\n17 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1451706014523982015)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Digital Country With All Things Real Countries Has\\n\\nSo i made a country digitally, so it has its own currency, flag, territory and fun activities to do like jobs or a shop or a chatting site or a bank, all this made in HTML+CSS+JS and Firebase, also you can even get a custom passport ALL FOR FREE heres the link pls review and give me a feedback https://revinoria-gov.netlify.app\\n\\nH\\n\\nℍ𝕪𝕡𝕖𝕣/ℍ𝕒𝕣𝕕𝕖𝕣\\n\\nCopy Paster!\\n\\n5 messages\\n\\n3 members\\n\\n17 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1451648625544270045)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Evaluating website\\n\\nArchived 16 days ago\\n\\nL\\n\\nLuna🌙\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n2 messages\\n\\n0 members\\n\\n18 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1451336494060146769)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Elo Based Poker Site\\n\\nHey everyone I built a chess inspired app to play with friends It’s build in next js. https://pokerino.io would love to get some feedback!\\n\\nS\\n\\nswupel\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n0 messages\\n\\n1 members