tes a Knowledge Graph of what you need to know and uses that as a curriculum to build your personalized learning path. Compas AGT learns from your learning patterns and psychometric data to deliver a uniquely personalized learning experience that adapts to you, not the other way around. This isn't just another chatbot. It's a fundamental shift in how we approach knowledge. This is Compas AGT, and it's here to help the next generation of the workforce upskill smarter. Compas AGT is currently in its Early Preview phase, available in select regions, with some areas potentially experiencing slower responses. As we continue refining and expanding its capabilities, you’ll notice the experience evolving rapidly with each new improvement and enhancement we roll out. Try agt.compasai.com right now!\\n\\nD\\n\\nd.bobola.ai\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n6 messages\\n\\n4 members\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1406381313514274917)\\n\\n[\\n\\n![Hey everyone!I built a Markdown note-taking app for students and creators 📚](/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.discordapp.com%2Fattachments%2F1406346077136879627%2F1406346077971415181%2F0.png%3Fex%3D695d5659%26is%3D695c04d9%26hm%3D027ced318f84677f1c9c83a5f63bf7896bdb6e21be136f8349278b5ab6cdb4f3%26&w=3840&q=75)\\n\\n### Hey everyone!I built a Markdown note-taking app for students and creators 📚\\n\\nArchived 4 months ago\\n\\nhtml & css go\\n\\nHey everyone! It’s a web-based note-taking app designed primarily for students, but also great for developers, content creators, and anyone who writes a lot. The goal is to offer a beautiful, intuitive interface and produce clean, well-formatted documents—without the frustration of traditional tools like Word. You can easily manage hundreds of notes, organize them into folders, export them, and boost your productivity with custom snippets, markdown shortcuts, and more. ## 🛠 Tech stack: - Frontend: Vue.js + Nuxt - Backend: Go - Storage: MinIO + MySQL I’m currently the only developer working on it, but I’d love to have contributors! Whether you’re into coding, UI/UX, documentation, or just want to share feedback and suggestions, you're very welcome to join 🫶 👉 GitHub repo: https://github.com/Smaug6739/Alexandrie If you like the idea, a ⭐ on GitHub would mean a lot — and feel free to reach out if you want to get involved!\\n\\nS\\n\\nExpress.js\\n\\n0 messages\\n\\n0 members\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1406346077136879627)\\n\\n[\\n\\n![My first red team project. Have mercy](/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.discordapp.com%2Fattachments%2F1406123852937039995%2F1406123853343621231%2FIMG_8059.png%3Fex%3D695d3023%26is%3D695bdea3%26hm%3D0a26a011216279ce003135375a1246c76997c84cbe446b237709ced562a9a614%26&w=3840&q=75)\\n\\n### My first red team project. Have mercy\\n\\nArchived 4 months ago\\n\\nI built a CRT-less manual map loader that’s only 4KB, handling relocations, imports, API hashing, syscall fallbacks, and stealth memory protections without relying on the C runtime. The loader carries an encrypted, embedded stage2 that’s 11KB and also CRT-less, it installs a root CA, sets the system proxy to an external server, and adds stealth layers like AMSI and ETW patching, NTDLL unhooking, and UAC elevation. Small footprint, no CRT overhead, fully obfuscated, and tuned for quiet execution. Each payload build is polymorphic due to encryption and section renaming.\\n\\nN\\n\\nVibe Coder!\\n\\n4 messages\\n\\n1 members\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1406123852937039995)\\n\\n[\\n\\n![🎨 SubSlay.app – Turn your text into color!](/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.discordapp.com%2Fattachments%2F1405938354985373747%2F1405938355287359562%2Fi_love_tree.png%3Fex%3D695d2c20%26is%3D695bdaa0%26hm%3D2fdaa4d61999e2d1accb88957c1e0279bfcbe908b212fa9856cf33cc3cdc0504%26&w=3840&q=75)\\n\\n### 🎨 SubSlay.app – Turn your text into color!\\n\\nArchived 4 months ago\\n\\nrust\\n\\nType anything, and every word gets its own unique hue. Make your messages pop, express vibes, or just have fun with colors — all instantly! 🌈\\n\\nA\\n\\nandria\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n7 messages\\n\\n2 members\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1405938354985373747)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Cybersecurity tool\\n\\nArchived 4 months ago\\n\\npython\\n\\nQuick cybersecurity tool for pentesting called Netra. terminal based tool pure py works on linux environments. It is a red team tool for network scanning spectically via mDNS. Feel free to dm for script\\n\\nJ\\n\\nJonas Savimbe\\n\\nScript Kiddie!\\n\\n1 messages\\n\\n2 members\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1405764488170311852)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Conquer server emulation\\n\\nArchived 4 months ago\\n\\nc#\\n\\nhttps://github.com/berniemackie97/OpenConquerPub Making an open source server emulation for an old game I used to play as a kid. It's been a fun experience reverse engineering the client to figure out the packet structures and communication encryptions. If anyone is interested in joining up or expanding on it it's fully open source. This has been pretty fun so far so if you have any other ideas or games you'd like to start a project doing this one I'd be more than happy to join!\\n\\nB\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n0 messages\\n\\n0 members\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1405407656033652736)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Guest blog service\\n\\nArchived 4 months ago\\n\\nR\\n\\nRamsey John\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n0 messages\\n\\n1 members\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1404997245044260904)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### Agentika File: Optimization Files using Artificial intelligence (AI)\\n\\nArchived 4 months ago\\n\\nHey everyone, I'd like to share a project I've been working on. ### \\\\*\\\\*Project Details\\\\*\\\\* \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Project Name:\\\\*\\\\* Agentika File 🤖 \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Brief Description:\\\\*\\\\* Agentika File is a smart web app that uses AI to automatically compress your files. Instead of just applying one setting, it acts as an intelligent agent that tries multiple strategies in a sequence until it successfully makes the file smaller. The entire process is transparent and happens privately in your browser. ### \\\\*\\\\*Tech Stack\\\\*\\\\* \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Frontend:\\\\*\\\\* React, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*AI Engine:\\\\*\\\\* Google Gemini 2.5-Flash with Structured Output \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Compression:\\\\*\\\\* The \\\\`browser-image-compression\\\\` library \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Core Architecture:\\\\*\\\\* Iterative Reduction Cascade (IRC) ### \\\\*\\\\*Key Features & Challenges Overcome\\\\*\\\\* The main goal was to solve the common frustration of \\\"file too large\\\" errors and the tedious trial-and-error of manual compression. \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Iterative Reduction Cascade (IRC):\\\\*\\\\* This is the core feature. The AI designs a \\\"ladder\\\" of compression strategies, from gentle to aggressive. If one attempt fails to reduce the file size, it automatically tries the next one. It doesn't give up. \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*100% Browser-Side Privacy:\\\\*\\\\* No files are ever uploaded to a server. All the processing is done directly in your browser, which means your data is completely private and the process is very fast. \\\\* \\\\*\\\\*Radical Transparency:\\\\*\\\\* You can watch the AI \\\"struggle\\\" in a live log. It shows you every attempt, failure, and which strategy finally succeeded. I'd love to hear your thoughts and any feedback you might have. Let me know what you think\\n\\nA\\n\\nArdelyo\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n2 messages\\n\\n3 members\\n\\n5 months ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1404787086552207452)\\n\\n[\\n\\n![QuickBrowse](/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.discordapp.com%2Fattachments%2F1404775268358422600%2F1404775269851467847%2Fimage.png%3Fex%3D695d8e2b%26is%3D695c3cab%26hm%3D556ea01d5a74d053d1c047d719ad781eb3b3fa6ac4aaab4bd770ba313228b43d