\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1455830180026388612)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### hi, i'm going to need 11 testers for my app so it can be published\\n\\nC\\n\\nRoi\\n\\nCopy Paster!\\n\\n25 messages\\n\\n3 members\\n\\n7 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1455251271849349286)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### yo guys check this out i made a .wav file in c\\n\\nc\\n\\nokay so this is lowkey really simple but i hadn't thought of this before. essentially a wav file is literally just a list of numbers that tell your speakers how much to move at each tiny interval in time. what im doing here is making sine waves with the math sin() funtion (the simplest tone). we just feed it the frequency we want and the current time, and it spits out a number between -1 and 1. then we convert those decimal numbers into 16-bit integers (numbers from -32,767 to 32,767) because that's what the wav format expects. each number represents how much the speaker cone should move at a given moment. the wav header at the beginning of the file is just metadata, after that its just wikipedia information and code lol\\n\\nZ\\n\\nchris\\n\\nVerified\\n\\n3 messages\\n\\n3 members\\n\\n10 days ago\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n](/en/community/showcase/1454324291213725811)\\n\\n[\\n\\n### What I learned in 1 day\\n\\nhtml & css\\n\\n<!DOCTYPE html> <html> <body> <h1>LearnSimply</h1> <p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Natus ducimus iusto ipsa similique aspernatur blanditiis voluptatum dolor. Architecto, nihil ut!</p> <hr> <ol> <li><a href=\\\"#c++\\\">C++</a></li> <li><a href=\\\"#java\\\">Java</a></li> <li><a href=\\\"#python\\\">Python</a></li> <li><a href=\\\"#html\\\">HTML</a></li> </ol> <h2 id=\\\"c++\\\">C++</h2> <p>Lorem ipsum dolor, sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Quam accusamus in expedita, necessitatibus molestiae sed officia temporibus numquam voluptas autem.</p> <h2 id=\\\"java\\\">Java</h2> <p>Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet consectetur adipisicing elit. Commodi aperiam dolor eve